    <div class="prose">
      <p>A tired garden or a cracked, weedy driveway drags a whole house down, and homeowners know it. What stops them acting is not being able to picture the finished result, or not knowing who to trust with it. A good ad fixes both: it shows them exactly what's possible and puts a company they trust in front of them at the right moment.</p>

      <h2>What the ads bring in</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Block paving, resin and tarmac driveways</li>
        <li>Patios, slabbing and paving</li>
        <li>Full garden transformations and landscaping</li>
        <li>Turfing, fencing and decking</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why real footage wins</h2>
      <p>This trade is made for video. A weed-covered driveway or an overgrown garden turning into something clean and finished is a transformation homeowners can't scroll past. So we use <strong>real footage of your jobs</strong>, filmed on site or from work you've already done, never stock. The before-and-after is the whole pitch, and it sells the job better than any photo.</p>

      <h2>What the funnel asks</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Is it a driveway, a patio, or a full garden?</li>
        <li>Rough size of the area, and the postcode?</li>
        <li>When are they looking to get it done?</li>
        <li>Name and the best number to reach them.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>That sorts the homeowners with a real job and a real budget from the ones after a quick cheap quote, so you're quoting work worth having.</p>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>
    </div>

